cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the main paper and the DOI assigned to this first deposit. No new DOI is preassigned in this file."
type: article
title: "Retuned translated probes and the conditional bound Λ < 0.116398 for the de Bruijn–Newman constant"
authors:
  - family-names: Raymond
    given-names: Dale James
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1682-8529"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
abstract: >-
  Assuming every nontrivial Riemann zeta zero has real part at most 7/8,
  a computer-assisted translated-probe comparison gives the exact ceiling
  0.116397726408291 for the de Bruijn-Newman constant. The proof uses
  retuned physical source bounds, matched finite logarithmic coefficients
  and 44 exact continuous-domain kernel certificates. Two 14899-step
  rational histories reproduce and pass a separate auditor. The external
  zero-free hypothesis is not established by the numerical checks.
keywords:
  - de Bruijn-Newman constant
  - Riemann zeta function
  - translated probes
  - interval arithmetic
  - exact polynomial certificates
  - conditional theorem
